1.25.0: lens and framing - denoise, distortion, devignette, straighten, trim

The second batch of input work, before the scene adjustments: the
input is prepared, and everything after sees that frame. denoise
blurs the color differences and leaves luminance exactly as it was
(the weighted sum of the differences is zero and a blur of zero is
zero), about 2 px per unit at full size, for high-ISO raw before the
grain models add theirs. distortion is a radial correction, + undoing
barrel (r' = r(1 - k r^2) in half-diagonals), - pincushion; devignette
lifts the corners by that many stops with r^2; rotate straightens in
degrees, + clockwise, on the same canvas with black corners; and
trimx/trimy/trimw/trimh cut a window of the frame in fractions before
the camera's format crop. Rotation, distortion and devignette are one
bilinear resample pass, threaded; all identity at 0, so renders
without them are byte-identical to 1.24.

The geometry reports the prepared frame and adds orig (the file's
frame), trim (where the prepared frame sits in it) and rot, so the
page's wipe lays the original over a straightened, trimmed render
turned about the file's center and offset by the trim; A and current
with different straightening compare by the difference. The scene key
table grows to 17 keys and every front end follows: --denoise and
friends on both CLIs, the recipe, the server's query, the wasm's
SCENE argument, DENOISE= and friends in super8ify, a Lens & framing
group in the page (the trim as four margins), brackets for straighten
and distortion. The CLI recipe reader's key list is sized for the
table (it had room for 16 and dropped the 17th).

Tests: core checks the trim's frame and geometry, rotation's
direction and black corners, distortion's pull at the edge, the
devignette on the flat blue plane, denoise spreading a speck's
chroma while luminance holds, the key table and the recipe; compat
round-trips the lens keys through a JPEG and checks the geometry
line; serve renders a lens query byte-identical to the CLI; wasm
checks the keys and geometry in the comment; the page test maps trim
margins to x,y,w,h; Chromium wipes a straightened, trimmed render
against the original, the left image turned 5 degrees, centers
coinciding.

